!Series_summary	"VCN-01 is a hyaluronidase-expressing oncolytic adenovirus that increases immune checkpoint antibody tumor uptake in mice. VCN-01 was evaluated with durvalumab in recurrent/metastatic head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (R/M HNSCC) patients refractory to anti-PD-(L)1"
!Series_overall_design	"Patients (n=20) received intravenous VCN-01 (3.3E12 viral particles (vp), low dose (LD), or 1.0E13 vp, high dose (HD)), plus durvalumab (1500 mg/q4w) concomitantly (VCN-01 + durvalumab on day 1; Arm I) or sequentially (VCN-01 on day -14 + durvalumab on day 1; Arm II). Six patients were enrolled in Arm I LD, eight in Arm II LD, and six in Arm II HD."
